  "proposed_paragraph": "A story can also become a set of instructions for voices and bodies. In Brundabanara Sheshadhupa, credited to Mahapatra Nilamani Sahu with dramatic adaptation by Bijay Kumar Satapathy, a crow’s call and voices from inside the house interrupt Raghu’s reading. Later, music accompanies a shift into a remembered scene; a radio bulletin brings news into the room. These printed directions make sound part of the storytelling.",
  "proposed_note": "Mahapatra Nilamani Sahu; dramatic adaptation by Bijay Kumar Satapathy, ‘Brundabanara Sheshadhupa’, in Bauribandhu Kar (ed.), Sahityasadhak Mohapatra Nilamani Sahu (2004), pp. 197–211, especially 197–198, 208 and 211.",
